{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914847511,"sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_510f706631c74f8e932824f1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/README.md","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ledgerly\n2: \n3: A small personal ledger (Python 3.11+, standard library only). Import bank statements, have them\n4: categorised by rules, and report income, expenses and balances per month.\n5: \n6: ```bash\n7: python -m ledgerly account add checking \"Joint account\" --iban \"NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00\"\n8: python -m ledgerly import march.csv --format rabo --account checking\n9: python -m ledgerly report income 2026-03 --compare\n10: python -m ledgerly report balance\n11: python -m unittest discover -s tests\n12: ```\n13: \n14: Statement formats: `generic`, `ing` and `rabo` (see `ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`). Foreign\n15: currencies are converted with the rates in `rates.csv` (`date,currency,rate`). The ledger is one\n16: JSON file (`ledger.json`).\n17: \n18: Importing never drops or invents money: a statement line that cannot be read stops the import with\n19: an error naming the file and line, and nothing from that file is added.\n\n(End of file - total 19 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# ledgerly\n\nA small personal ledger (Python 3.11+, standard library only). Import bank statements, have them\ncategorised by rules, and report income, expenses and balances per month.\n\n```bash\npython -m ledgerly account add checking \"Joint account\" --iban \"NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00\"\npython -m ledgerly import march.csv --format rabo --account checking\npython -m ledgerly report income 2026-03 --compare\npython -m ledgerly report balance\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\nStatement formats: `generic`, `ing` and `rabo` (see `ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`). Foreign\ncurrencies are converted with the rates in `rates.csv` (`date,currency,rate`). The ledger is one\nJSON file (`ledger.json`).\n\nImporting never drops or invents money: a statement line that cannot be read stops the import with\nan error naming the file and line, and nothing from that file is added.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/README.md","text":"# ledgerly\n\nA small personal ledger (Python 3.11+, standard library only). Import bank statements, have them\ncategorised by rules, and report income, expenses and balances per month.\n\n```bash\npython -m ledgerly account add checking \"Joint account\" --iban \"NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00\"\npython -m ledgerly import march.csv --format rabo --account checking\npython -m ledgerly report income 2026-03 --compare\npython -m ledgerly report balance\npython -m unittest discover -s tests\n```\n\nStatement formats: `generic`, `ing` and `rabo` (see `ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`). Foreign\ncurrencies are converted with the rates in `rates.csv` (`date,currency,rate`). The ledger is one\nJSON file (`ledger.json`).\n\nImporting never drops or invents money: a statement line that cannot be read stops the import with\nan error naming the file and line, and nothing from that file is added.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":19,"totalLines":19,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794914847483,"end":1794914847496}},"id":"prt_1e9430afa001L96H3Bl1f7s08q","sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","messageID":"msg_1e9430137001AY5XNZSeNCzqDw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914847511,"sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_5ad99ac6935d40cc9260d15d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import unittest\n2: from datetime import date\n3: from decimal import Decimal\n4: \n5: from ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\n6: from ledgerly.io.bank_formats import parse_amount\n7: from ledgerly.io.csv_import import import_statement, read_statement\n8: from ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n9: \n10: from tests.helpers import journal, write\n11: \n12: GENERIC = \"\"\"date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban\n13: 2026-03-01,-42.10,EUR,Weekly shop,Albert Heijn 1234,\n14: 2026-03-02,+2500.00,EUR,Salary March,Acme BV,NL91ABNA0417164300\n15: \"\"\"\n16: \n17: ING = \"\"\"Datum;Naam / Omschrijving;Tegenrekening;Af Bij;Bedrag (EUR);Mededelingen\n18: 20260303;Spotify AB;;Af;9,99;Ref: 7781\n19: 20260304;Gemeente Utrecht;NL91ABNA0417164300;Bij;1.234,56;Teruggave\n20: \"\"\"\n21: \n22: RABO = \"\"\"Datum,Bedrag,Munt,Naam tegenpartij,Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN,Omschrijving-1\n23: 2026-03-01,,EUR,,,Saldo begin\n24: 2026-03-05,\"-12,50\",EUR,Jumbo Utrecht,,Boodschappen\n25: 2026-03-06,\"-1.020,00\",EUR,Woonstichting,NL91ABNA0417164300,Huur maart\n26: \"\"\"\n27: \n28: \n29: class AmountTest(unittest.TestCase):\n30:     def test_decimal_comma(self):\n31:         self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"1.234,56\", decimal_comma=True), Decimal(\"1234.56\"))\n32:         self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"-12,50\", decimal_comma=True), Decimal(\"-12.50\"))\n33:         self.assertIsNone(parse_amount(\"  \", decimal_comma=True))\n34: \n35:     def test_decimal_point(self):\n36:         self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"+1,250.00\", decimal_comma=False), Decimal(\"1250.00\"))\n37:         self.assertIsNone(parse_amount(\"abc\", decimal_comma=False))\n38: \n39: \n40: class FormatTest(unittest.TestCase):\n41:     def test_generic(self):\n42:         rows = read_statement(write(GENERIC), \"generic\", \"checking\")\n43:         self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-42.10\"), Decimal(\"2500.00\")])\n44:         self.assertEqual(rows[1].source, \"statement.csv:3\")\n45: \n46:     def test_ing_signs_from_af_bij(self):\n47:         rows = read_statement(write(ING), \"ing\", \"checking\")\n48:         self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-9.99\"), Decimal(\"1234.56\")])\n49:         self.assertEqual(rows[0].description, \"Spotify AB\")\n50:         self.assertEqual(rows[1].booked, date(2026, 3, 4))\n51: \n52:     def test_rabo_skips_balance_lines(self):\n53:         rows = read_statement(write(RABO), \"rabo\", \"checking\")\n54:         self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-12.50\"), Decimal(\"-1020.00\")])\n55: \n56:     def test_errors_name_the_line(self):\n57:         bad = GENERIC.replace(\"-42.10\", \"lots\")\n58:         with self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, \"statement.csv:2\"):\n59:             read_statement(write(bad), \"generic\", \"checking\")\n60:         with self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, \"unknown format\"):\n61:             read_statement(write(GENERIC), \"abn\", \"checking\")\n62: \n63: \n64: class ImportTest(unittest.TestCase):\n65:     def test_import_categorises_and_deduplicates(self):\n66:         book = journal()\n67:         path = write(RABO)\n68:         first = import_statement(book, path, \"rabo\", \"checking\", Categorizer([]))\n69:         again = import_statement(book, path, \"rabo\", \"checking\", Categorizer([]))\n70:         self.assertEqual((first.added, again.added, again.duplicates), (2, 0, 2))\n71:         self.assertEqual(sorted(t.category for t in book), [\"groceries\", \"rent\"])\n72: \n73: \n74: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n75:     unittest.main()\n\n(End of file - total 75 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.io.bank_formats import parse_amount\nfrom ledgerly.io.csv_import import import_statement, read_statement\nfrom ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n\nfrom tests.helpers import journal, write\n\nGENERIC = \"\"\"date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban\n2026-03-01,-42.10,EUR,Weekly shop,Albert Heijn 1234,\n2026-03-02,+2500.00,EUR,Salary March,Acme BV,NL91ABNA0417164300\n\"\"\"\n\nING = \"\"\"Datum;Naam / Omschrijving;Tegenrekening;Af Bij;Bedrag (EUR);Mededelingen\n20260303;Spotify AB;;Af;9,99;Ref: 7781\n20260304;Gemeente Utrecht;NL91ABNA0417164300;Bij;1.234,56;Teruggave\n\"\"\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_import.py","text":"import unittest\nfrom datetime import date\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.io.bank_formats import parse_amount\nfrom ledgerly.io.csv_import import import_statement, read_statement\nfrom ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n\nfrom tests.helpers import journal, write\n\nGENERIC = \"\"\"date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban\n2026-03-01,-42.10,EUR,Weekly shop,Albert Heijn 1234,\n2026-03-02,+2500.00,EUR,Salary March,Acme BV,NL91ABNA0417164300\n\"\"\"\n\nING = \"\"\"Datum;Naam / Omschrijving;Tegenrekening;Af Bij;Bedrag (EUR);Mededelingen\n20260303;Spotify AB;;Af;9,99;Ref: 7781\n20260304;Gemeente Utrecht;NL91ABNA0417164300;Bij;1.234,56;Teruggave\n\"\"\"\n\nRABO = \"\"\"Datum,Bedrag,Munt,Naam tegenpartij,Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN,Omschrijving-1\n2026-03-01,,EUR,,,Saldo begin\n2026-03-05,\"-12,50\",EUR,Jumbo Utrecht,,Boodschappen\n2026-03-06,\"-1.020,00\",EUR,Woonstichting,NL91ABNA0417164300,Huur maart\n\"\"\"\n\n\nclass AmountTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_decimal_comma(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"1.234,56\", decimal_comma=True), Decimal(\"1234.56\"))\n        self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"-12,50\", decimal_comma=True), Decimal(\"-12.50\"))\n        self.assertIsNone(parse_amount(\"  \", decimal_comma=True))\n\n    def test_decimal_point(self):\n        self.assertEqual(parse_amount(\"+1,250.00\", decimal_comma=False), Decimal(\"1250.00\"))\n        self.assertIsNone(parse_amount(\"abc\", decimal_comma=False))\n\n\nclass FormatTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_generic(self):\n        rows = read_statement(write(GENERIC), \"generic\", \"checking\")\n        self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-42.10\"), Decimal(\"2500.00\")])\n        self.assertEqual(rows[1].source, \"statement.csv:3\")\n\n    def test_ing_signs_from_af_bij(self):\n        rows = read_statement(write(ING), \"ing\", \"checking\")\n        self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-9.99\"), Decimal(\"1234.56\")])\n        self.assertEqual(rows[0].description, \"Spotify AB\")\n        self.assertEqual(rows[1].booked, date(2026, 3, 4))\n\n    def test_rabo_skips_balance_lines(self):\n        rows = read_statement(write(RABO), \"rabo\", \"checking\")\n        self.assertEqual([r.amount for r in rows], [Decimal(\"-12.50\"), Decimal(\"-1020.00\")])\n\n    def test_errors_name_the_line(self):\n        bad = GENERIC.replace(\"-42.10\", \"lots\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, \"statement.csv:2\"):\n            read_statement(write(bad), \"generic\", \"checking\")\n        with self.assertRaisesRegex(ImportError_, \"unknown format\"):\n            read_statement(write(GENERIC), \"abn\", \"checking\")\n\n\nclass ImportTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_import_categorises_and_deduplicates(self):\n        book = journal()\n        path = write(RABO)\n        first = import_statement(book, path, \"rabo\", \"checking\", Categorizer([]))\n        again = import_statement(book, path, \"rabo\", \"checking\", Categorizer([]))\n        self.assertEqual((first.added, again.added, again.duplicates), (2, 0, 2))\n        self.assertEqual(sorted(t.category for t in book), [\"groceries\", \"rent\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":75,"totalLines":75,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/test_import.py","time":{"start":1794914847479,"end":1794914847497}},"id":"prt_1e9430af50010mxMA9O7frBjy7","sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","messageID":"msg_1e9430137001AY5XNZSeNCzqDw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914847511,"sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_f16d4537bca346a19d66082f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import contextlib\n2: import io\n3: import tempfile\n4: import unittest\n5: from pathlib import Path\n6: \n7: from ledgerly.__main__ import run\n8: \n9: from tests.test_import import ING\n10: \n11: \n12: class CliTest(unittest.TestCase):\n13:     def setUp(self):\n14:         self.dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"ledgerly-cli-\"))\n15:         self.ledger = str(self.dir / \"ledger.json\")\n16: \n17:     def ledgerly(self, *args: str) -> str:\n18:         out = io.StringIO()\n19:         with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out):\n20:             self.assertEqual(run([\"--ledger\", self.ledger, \"--rates\", str(self.dir / \"r.csv\"), *args]), 0)\n21:         return out.getvalue()\n22: \n23:     def test_import_and_report(self):\n24:         (self.dir / \"ing.csv\").write_text(ING)\n25:         self.ledgerly(\"account\", \"add\", \"checking\", \"Checking\")\n26:         self.assertIn(\"2 added\", self.ledgerly(\"import\", str(self.dir / \"ing.csv\"), \"--format\", \"ing\", \"--account\", \"checking\"))\n27:         report = self.ledgerly(\"report\", \"income\", \"2026-03\")\n28:         self.assertIn(\"Subscriptions\", report)\n29:         self.assertIn(\"Net                         1,224.57 EUR\", report)\n30: \n31: \n32: if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n33:     unittest.main()\n\n(End of file - total 33 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import contextlib\nimport io\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom ledgerly.__main__ import run\n\nfrom tests.test_import import ING\n\n\nclass CliTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"ledgerly-cli-\"))\n        self.ledger = str(self.dir / \"ledger.json\")\n\n    def ledgerly(self, *args: str) -> str:\n        out = io.StringIO()\n        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out):\n            self.assertEqual(run([\"--ledger\", self.ledger, \"--rates\", str(self.dir / \"r.csv\"), *args]), 0)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_cli.py","text":"import contextlib\nimport io\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom ledgerly.__main__ import run\n\nfrom tests.test_import import ING\n\n\nclass CliTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"ledgerly-cli-\"))\n        self.ledger = str(self.dir / \"ledger.json\")\n\n    def ledgerly(self, *args: str) -> str:\n        out = io.StringIO()\n        with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out):\n            self.assertEqual(run([\"--ledger\", self.ledger, \"--rates\", str(self.dir / \"r.csv\"), *args]), 0)\n        return out.getvalue()\n\n    def test_import_and_report(self):\n        (self.dir / \"ing.csv\").write_text(ING)\n        self.ledgerly(\"account\", \"add\", \"checking\", \"Checking\")\n        self.assertIn(\"2 added\", self.ledgerly(\"import\", str(self.dir / \"ing.csv\"), \"--format\", \"ing\", \"--account\", \"checking\"))\n        report = self.ledgerly(\"report\", \"income\", \"2026-03\")\n        self.assertIn(\"Subscriptions\", report)\n        self.assertIn(\"Net                         1,224.57 EUR\", report)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":33,"totalLines":33,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/test_cli.py","time":{"start":1794914847481,"end":1794914847498}},"id":"prt_1e9430af8001hKicMlXeRWeGkf","sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","messageID":"msg_1e9430137001AY5XNZSeNCzqDw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914847511,"sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_3ef23b7b16214831bcdf89dc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","offset":1,"limit":260},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n2: \n3: Every reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\n4: yields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n5: \n6: - ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n7:   sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n8: - ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n9:   ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n10:   comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n11: - ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n12:   dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n13:   ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n14: \"\"\"\n15: \n16: from __future__ import annotations\n17: \n18: import re\n19: from collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\n20: from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n21: \n22: from ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\n23: from ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\n24: from ledgerly.util.dates import parse_bank_date\n25: from ledgerly.util.text import squash, strip_reference\n26: \n27: Row = tuple[int, dict[str, str]]\n28: Reader = Callable[[Iterable[Row], str, str], Iterator[Transaction]]\n29: \n30: # 1.234,56 or 12,50 with an optional minus: how Dutch banks write amounts.\n31: EURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n32: \n33: \n34: def parse_amount(text: str, *, decimal_comma: bool) -> Decimal | None:\n35:     \"\"\"The amount in a statement cell, or ``None`` when the cell holds no amount.\n36: \n37:     ``decimal_comma``: ``1.234,56`` (Dutch banks); otherwise ``1234.56``.\n38:     \"\"\"\n39: \n40:     cleaned = text.strip().replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n41:     if not cleaned:\n42:         return None\n43:     if decimal_comma:\n44:         if not EURO_AMOUNT.match(cleaned):\n45:             return None\n46:         return Decimal(cleaned.replace(\".\", \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"))\n47:     try:\n48:         value = Decimal(cleaned.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n49:     except InvalidOperation:\n50:         return None\n51:     return value if value.is_finite() else None\n52: \n53: \n54: def _field(row: dict[str, str], name: str, source: str, line: int) -> str:\n55:     if name not in row or row[name] is None:\n56:         raise ImportError_(f\"missing column {name!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n57:     return row[name]\n58: \n59: \n60: def _date(text: str, source: str, line: int, formats: tuple[str, ...]):  # noqa: ANN202\n61:     try:\n62:         return parse_bank_date(text, formats=formats)\n63:     except ValueError as exc:\n64:         raise ImportError_(str(exc), source=source, line=line) from None\n65: \n66: \n67: def read_generic(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n68:     for line, row in rows:\n69:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"amount\", source, line), decimal_comma=False)\n70:         if amount is None:\n71:             raise ImportError_(f\"cannot read the amount {row['amount']!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n72:         yield Transaction(\n73:             account=account,\n74:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"date\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n75:             amount=amount,\n76:             currency=(row.get(\"currency\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n77:             description=squash(row.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n78:             counterparty=squash(row.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n79:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"iban\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n80:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n81:         )\n82: \n83: \n84: def read_ing(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n85:     for line, row in rows:\n86:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag (EUR)\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n87:         if amount is None:\n88:             raise ImportError_(\n89:                 f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag (EUR)']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n90:             )\n91:         direction = _field(row, \"Af Bij\", source, line).strip()\n92:         if direction not in (\"Af\", \"Bij\"):\n93:             raise ImportError_(f\"Af Bij must be Af or Bij, not {direction!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n94:         name = squash(_field(row, \"Naam / Omschrijving\", source, line))\n95:         notes = strip_reference(row.get(\"Mededelingen\", \"\"))\n96:         yield Transaction(\n97:             account=account,\n98:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y%m%d\",)),\n99:             amount=-amount if direction == \"Af\" else amount,\n100:             currency=\"EUR\",\n101:             description=f\"{name} {notes}\".strip(),\n102:             counterparty=name,\n103:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n104:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n105:         )\n106: \n107: \n108: def _is_balance_line(row: dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n109:     return (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n110: \n111: \n112: def read_rabo(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n113:     for line, row in rows:\n114:         amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n115:         if amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n116:             continue\n117:         yield Transaction(\n118:             account=account,\n119:             booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n120:             amount=amount,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n121:             currency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n122:             description=strip_reference(row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\", \"\")),\n123:             counterparty=squash(row.get(\"Naam tegenpartij\", \"\")),\n124:             counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n125:             source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n126:         )\n127: \n128: \n129: READERS: dict[str, Reader] = {\"generic\": read_generic, \"ing\": read_ing, \"rabo\": read_rabo}\n130: DELIMITERS = {\"generic\": \",\", \"ing\": \";\", \"rabo\": \",\"}\n\n(End of file - total 130 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n\nEvery reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\nyields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n\n- ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n  sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n- ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n  ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n  comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n- ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n  dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n  ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","text":"\"\"\"The bank statement formats ledgerly reads, one reader per bank.\n\nEvery reader takes the rows of a CSV file (as dictionaries, with the 1-based file line number) and\nyields ``Transaction`` objects for one account. Formats:\n\n- ``generic``: ``date,amount,currency,description,counterparty,iban`` with a decimal point and a\n  sign (``-12.50``, ``+1250.00``).\n- ``ing``: ING's export: ``Datum`` (YYYYMMDD), ``Naam / Omschrijving``, ``Tegenrekening``,\n  ``Af Bij`` (``Af``: money out, ``Bij``: money in), ``Bedrag (EUR)`` (always positive, decimal\n  comma), ``Mededelingen``.\n- ``rabo``: Rabobank's export: ``Datum`` (YYYY-MM-DD), ``Bedrag`` (signed, decimal comma, thousands\n  dots: ``-12,50``, ``+1.250,00``), ``Munt``, ``Naam tegenpartij``, ``Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN``,\n  ``Omschrijving-1``. Balance lines (``Saldo ...``) carry no amount and are skipped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Iterator\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.util.dates import parse_bank_date\nfrom ledgerly.util.text import squash, strip_reference\n\nRow = tuple[int, dict[str, str]]\nReader = Callable[[Iterable[Row], str, str], Iterator[Transaction]]\n\n# 1.234,56 or 12,50 with an optional minus: how Dutch banks write amounts.\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n\n\ndef parse_amount(text: str, *, decimal_comma: bool) -> Decimal | None:\n    \"\"\"The amount in a statement cell, or ``None`` when the cell holds no amount.\n\n    ``decimal_comma``: ``1.234,56`` (Dutch banks); otherwise ``1234.56``.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    cleaned = text.strip().replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n    if not cleaned:\n        return None\n    if decimal_comma:\n        if not EURO_AMOUNT.match(cleaned):\n            return None\n        return Decimal(cleaned.replace(\".\", \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"))\n    try:\n        value = Decimal(cleaned.replace(\",\", \"\"))\n    except InvalidOperation:\n        return None\n    return value if value.is_finite() else None\n\n\ndef _field(row: dict[str, str], name: str, source: str, line: int) -> str:\n    if name not in row or row[name] is None:\n        raise ImportError_(f\"missing column {name!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n    return row[name]\n\n\ndef _date(text: str, source: str, line: int, formats: tuple[str, ...]):  # noqa: ANN202\n    try:\n        return parse_bank_date(text, formats=formats)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        raise ImportError_(str(exc), source=source, line=line) from None\n\n\ndef read_generic(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"amount\", source, line), decimal_comma=False)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(f\"cannot read the amount {row['amount']!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"date\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,\n            currency=(row.get(\"currency\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=squash(row.get(\"description\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"counterparty\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"iban\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef read_ing(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag (EUR)\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None:\n            raise ImportError_(\n                f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag (EUR)']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n            )\n        direction = _field(row, \"Af Bij\", source, line).strip()\n        if direction not in (\"Af\", \"Bij\"):\n            raise ImportError_(f\"Af Bij must be Af or Bij, not {direction!r}\", source=source, line=line)\n        name = squash(_field(row, \"Naam / Omschrijving\", source, line))\n        notes = strip_reference(row.get(\"Mededelingen\", \"\"))\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y%m%d\",)),\n            amount=-amount if direction == \"Af\" else amount,\n            currency=\"EUR\",\n            description=f\"{name} {notes}\".strip(),\n            counterparty=name,\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\ndef _is_balance_line(row: dict[str, str]) -> bool:\n    return (row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\") or \"\").strip().lower().startswith(\"saldo\")\n\n\ndef read_rabo(rows: Iterable[Row], account: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Transaction]:\n    for line, row in rows:\n        amount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\n        if amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n            continue\n        yield Transaction(\n            account=account,\n            booked=_date(_field(row, \"Datum\", source, line), source, line, (\"%Y-%m-%d\",)),\n            amount=amount,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\n            currency=(row.get(\"Munt\") or \"EUR\").strip().upper(),\n            description=strip_reference(row.get(\"Omschrijving-1\", \"\")),\n            counterparty=squash(row.get(\"Naam tegenpartij\", \"\")),\n            counter_iban=(row.get(\"Tegenrekening IBAN/BBAN\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            source=f\"{source}:{line}\",\n        )\n\n\nREADERS: dict[str, Reader] = {\"generic\": read_generic, \"ing\": read_ing, \"rabo\": read_rabo}\nDELIMITERS = {\"generic\": \",\", \"ing\": \";\", \"rabo\": \",\"}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":130,"totalLines":130,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py","time":{"start":1794914847473,"end":1794914847499}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Need inspect exact files. User statement salary +2.750,00. Root likely plus regex. They say import 3 read 3 added despite 4 rows where first saldo blank skipped = 3 tx. Positive salary likely parsed None, causing crash. Need fix plus and perhaps ensure unreadable rows error atomic. Requirements explicit if cannot read line, import stop error names file/line add nothing. Existing read_rabo only handles blank balance, malformed nonbalance None. Need implement robust. Also statement \"Everything works today same.\" Need tests. We need understand code and conventions. Read bank_formats, csv_import, tests, README, main maybe tx. Parallel.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e9430aee001SPE90iTr9Xcwco","sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","messageID":"msg_1e9430137001AY5XNZSeNCzqDw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914847511,"sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_269a742021344e7aa4ae2b4e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"Importing a statement file into the journal: read, categorise, de-duplicate.\"\"\"\n2: \n3: from __future__ import annotations\n4: \n5: import csv\n6: import io\n7: from collections.abc import Iterator\n8: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n9: from pathlib import Path\n10: \n11: from ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\n12: from ledgerly.core.journal import Journal\n13: from ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\n14: from ledgerly.io.bank_formats import DELIMITERS, READERS, Row\n15: from ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n16: \n17: ENCODINGS = (\"utf-8-sig\", \"cp1252\")\n18: MAX_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024\n19: \n20: \n21: @dataclass\n22: class ImportResult:\n23:     source: str\n24:     read: int = 0\n25:     added: int = 0\n26:     duplicates: int = 0\n27:     uncategorised: int = 0\n28:     warnings: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n29: \n30:     def summary(self) -> str:\n31:         parts = [f\"{self.added} added\", f\"{self.duplicates} already there\"]\n32:         if self.uncategorised:\n33:             parts.append(f\"{self.uncategorised} uncategorised\")\n34:         return f\"{self.source}: {self.read} read, \" + \", \".join(parts)\n35: \n36: \n37: def decode(data: bytes, source: str) -> str:\n38:     for encoding in ENCODINGS:\n39:         try:\n40:             return data.decode(encoding)\n41:         except UnicodeDecodeError:\n42:             continue\n43:     raise ImportError_(\"the file is neither UTF-8 nor Windows-1252 text\", source=source)\n44: \n45: \n46: def rows(text: str, delimiter: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Row]:\n47:     reader = csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\"), delimiter=delimiter)\n48:     if not reader.fieldnames:\n49:         raise ImportError_(\"the file is empty\", source=source)\n50:     for row in reader:\n51:         if None in row:\n52:             raise ImportError_(\n53:                 f\"{len(row[None])} more field(s) than the header\", source=source, line=reader.line_num\n54:             )\n55:         if not any((value or \"\").strip() for value in row.values()):\n56:             continue\n57:         yield reader.line_num, {k.strip(): (v or \"\") for k, v in row.items() if k}\n58: \n59: \n60: def read_statement(path: Path, fmt: str, account: str) -> list[Transaction]:\n61:     if fmt not in READERS:\n62:         raise ImportError_(f\"unknown format {fmt!r} (use {', '.join(READERS)})\", source=path.name)\n63:     try:\n64:         data = path.read_bytes()\n65:     except OSError:\n66:         raise ImportError_(\"cannot read the file\", source=path.name) from None\n67:     if len(data) > MAX_BYTES:\n68:         raise ImportError_(\"the file is larger than 20 MB\", source=path.name)\n69:     text = decode(data, path.name)\n70:     return list(READERS[fmt](rows(text, DELIMITERS[fmt], path.name), account, path.name))\n71: \n72: \n73: def import_statement(\n74:     journal: Journal, path: Path, fmt: str, account: str, categorizer: Categorizer\n75: ) -> ImportResult:\n76:     \"\"\"Add the statement's transactions to ``journal`` (all of them, or none on an error).\"\"\"\n77: \n78:     result = ImportResult(source=path.name)\n79:     transactions = read_statement(path, fmt, account)\n80:     result.read = len(transactions)\n81:     known = {t.currency for t in transactions} - {journal.chart.get(account).currency}\n82:     if known:\n83:         result.warnings.append(\n84:             f\"{path.name} has amounts in {', '.join(sorted(known))}; reports convert them\"\n85:         )\n86:     categorised = []\n87:     for transaction in transactions:\n88:         category = categorizer.category_for(transaction)\n89:         if category == \"uncategorised\":\n90:             result.uncategorised += 1\n91:         categorised.append(transaction.categorised(category))\n92:     result.added, result.duplicates = journal.extend(categorised)\n93:     return result\n\n(End of file - total 93 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"Importing a statement file into the journal: read, categorise, de-duplicate.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport io\nfrom collections.abc import Iterator\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.journal import Journal\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.io.bank_formats import DELIMITERS, READERS, Row\nfrom ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n\nENCODINGS = (\"utf-8-sig\", \"cp1252\")\nMAX_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024\n\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-1/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py","text":"\"\"\"Importing a statement file into the journal: read, categorise, de-duplicate.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport io\nfrom collections.abc import Iterator\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom ledgerly.core.errors import ImportError_\nfrom ledgerly.core.journal import Journal\nfrom ledgerly.core.transactions import Transaction\nfrom ledgerly.io.bank_formats import DELIMITERS, READERS, Row\nfrom ledgerly.rules.categorize import Categorizer\n\nENCODINGS = (\"utf-8-sig\", \"cp1252\")\nMAX_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass ImportResult:\n    source: str\n    read: int = 0\n    added: int = 0\n    duplicates: int = 0\n    uncategorised: int = 0\n    warnings: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n    def summary(self) -> str:\n        parts = [f\"{self.added} added\", f\"{self.duplicates} already there\"]\n        if self.uncategorised:\n            parts.append(f\"{self.uncategorised} uncategorised\")\n        return f\"{self.source}: {self.read} read, \" + \", \".join(parts)\n\n\ndef decode(data: bytes, source: str) -> str:\n    for encoding in ENCODINGS:\n        try:\n            return data.decode(encoding)\n        except UnicodeDecodeError:\n            continue\n    raise ImportError_(\"the file is neither UTF-8 nor Windows-1252 text\", source=source)\n\n\ndef rows(text: str, delimiter: str, source: str) -> Iterator[Row]:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\"), delimiter=delimiter)\n    if not reader.fieldnames:\n        raise ImportError_(\"the file is empty\", source=source)\n    for row in reader:\n        if None in row:\n            raise ImportError_(\n                f\"{len(row[None])} more field(s) than the header\", source=source, line=reader.line_num\n            )\n        if not any((value or \"\").strip() for value in row.values()):\n            continue\n        yield reader.line_num, {k.strip(): (v or \"\") for k, v in row.items() if k}\n\n\ndef read_statement(path: Path, fmt: str, account: str) -> list[Transaction]:\n    if fmt not in READERS:\n        raise ImportError_(f\"unknown format {fmt!r} (use {', '.join(READERS)})\", source=path.name)\n    try:\n        data = path.read_bytes()\n    except OSError:\n        raise ImportError_(\"cannot read the file\", source=path.name) from None\n    if len(data) > MAX_BYTES:\n        raise ImportError_(\"the file is larger than 20 MB\", source=path.name)\n    text = decode(data, path.name)\n    return list(READERS[fmt](rows(text, DELIMITERS[fmt], path.name), account, path.name))\n\n\ndef import_statement(\n    journal: Journal, path: Path, fmt: str, account: str, categorizer: Categorizer\n) -> ImportResult:\n    \"\"\"Add the statement's transactions to ``journal`` (all of them, or none on an error).\"\"\"\n\n    result = ImportResult(source=path.name)\n    transactions = read_statement(path, fmt, account)\n    result.read = len(transactions)\n    known = {t.currency for t in transactions} - {journal.chart.get(account).currency}\n    if known:\n        result.warnings.append(\n            f\"{path.name} has amounts in {', '.join(sorted(known))}; reports convert them\"\n        )\n    categorised = []\n    for transaction in transactions:\n        category = categorizer.category_for(transaction)\n        if category == \"uncategorised\":\n            result.uncategorised += 1\n        categorised.append(transaction.categorised(category))\n    result.added, result.duplicates = journal.extend(categorised)\n    return result","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":93,"totalLines":93,"truncated":false}},"title":"ledgerly/io/csv_import.py","time":{"start":1794914847476,"end":1794914847506}},"id":"prt_1e9430af2001f4x8nF7ZMRDCzd","sessionID":"ses_e16bf3244ffe3dp0Kl8aoaMvCb","messageID":"msg_1e9430137001AY5XNZSeNCzqDw"}}
